    // ---- computed fields, found by matching values ----
    // The engine's field table names these but gives them no offset: they are served by a getter,
    // so there is nothing in the table to read. What is here was found the other way round - the
    // game was asked for each by name across 384 weapons, and this is the offset carrying the
    // matching value for every weapon the dump and the pool both name.
    //
    // Only 72 weapons are named the same way in both, so these rest on fewer witnesses than the
    // fields taken from the table. They are kept because the values vary enough that agreement
    // across all 72 is not something a wrong offset does: maxdamage takes fifteen distinct values,
    // firstraisetime nine.
    //
    // maxdamagerange and mindamagerange are NOT here on purpose. They matched 0x680 and 0x694,
    // which are the first and sixth stops of the damageRange curve already named at 0x680 - the
    // ends of a run, not fields of their own.
    //
    // firstraisetime is a state timer, which the earlier note in this project called unplaceable
    // on the grounds that the engine does not report such things to script. It does.
    // Rechecked in the dump (2026-10-22) with the script field table's accessor read right (the qword
    // 24 bytes after the hash): firstRaiseTime -> 7ff7916d88c0 -> tunables 0xd20 (unless an
    // attachment overrides), maxAmmo -> 0xd4c (x clip size when 0x10bf is set).

    {"offset": "0xd20", "name": "firstraisetime", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 975, "agreed": 72, "examples": []},
    {"offset": "0xd4c", "name": "maxammo", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 718, "agreed": 72, "examples": []},
    {"offset": "0xbec", "name": "maxdamage", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 859, "agreed": 72, "examples": []},

